{
  "name": "spoonbill",
  "kind": "parts",
  "_about": "a Eurasian spoonbill wading: all white, the long flat black bill spreading at its end into the round spatula, tipped yellow; the shaggy nuchal crest of the breeding bird and the buff wash on the breast; long black legs. Coat: the roseate spoonbill -- pink, the carmine shoulder, the orange tail, the bare greenish head, no crest (2026-11-08, tools/creaturegen/sweep/necks.py) The NECK is one `sweep` (sculpt.js) along the chain of neck bones, not a tube a bone blended into the next: no bead at the joints. (2026-11-08, tools/creaturegen/sweep/flynecks.py) ALOFT the neck is held nearly straight ahead with a slight sag: the neck sweep is skinned from the body along its bones with its hand-offs on the rest curve's bends (`knotsAt`, `spread`), and the neck bones' and head's `flyRot` set with them.",
